WEBVTT

00:00:00.592 --> 00:00:02.372
This is the task from our call.

00:00:02.732 --> 00:00:05.212
A student leaves a private note for their advisor.

00:00:05.492 --> 00:00:07.832
It must never be sent to an AI model.

00:00:08.092 --> 00:00:11.712
Make the smallest safe change, and show how you verify it.

00:00:12.764 --> 00:00:15.844
Pathways helps a student pick a next step after high school.

00:00:16.224 --> 00:00:18.024
This planner already existed.

00:00:18.304 --> 00:00:22.924
Code chooses the step, and a language model supplies the wording through one file,

00:00:23.084 --> 00:00:23.924
the gateway.

00:00:24.244 --> 00:00:26.824
Here that model is a scripted stand-in.

00:00:28.832 --> 00:00:31.472
The note box and the gateway already existed.

00:00:31.812 --> 00:00:35.572
Three things were missing: a way for an advisor to read the note,

00:00:35.792 --> 00:00:40.382
protection against printing it by accident, and a test that watches model calls

00:00:40.412 --> 00:00:41.932
made outside the gateway.

00:00:42.552 --> 00:00:43.832
Dani writes a note.

00:00:44.232 --> 00:00:46.092
Everything in it is invented.

00:00:49.059 --> 00:00:53.819
A small detector model, running in her browser, finds the phone number and the email,

00:00:53.939 --> 00:00:55.559
and suggests leaving them out.

00:00:55.899 --> 00:00:57.359
She sends it as it is.

00:00:59.004 --> 00:01:00.844
This is the advisor inbox.

00:01:01.184 --> 00:01:03.984
In this demo it is public, with no sign-in.

00:01:04.244 --> 00:01:07.884
The students are invented, and no real advisor receives anything.

00:01:08.484 --> 00:01:12.204
The list leaves the note out, and so does opening a request.

00:01:12.604 --> 00:01:17.504
Open the note is the one route that returns it, and each open is recorded.

00:01:17.904 --> 00:01:22.474
Names and contact details stay hidden on screen until the advisor switches that

00:01:22.504 --> 00:01:23.404
kind on.

00:01:27.108 --> 00:01:29.308
The boundary is two layers of code.

00:01:29.648 --> 00:01:32.908
First, the server seals the note before it queues it.

00:01:33.228 --> 00:01:38.138
As JSON, as a string, or in an error, it prints as the word private,

00:01:38.168 --> 00:01:39.008
in brackets.

00:01:39.448 --> 00:01:41.388
Only the advisor route opens it.

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:45.028
That prevents accidental printing, not deliberate access.

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:47.141
Second, the gateway.

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:51.741
It checks a plain copy of each payload and accepts only listed codes,

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:54.721
record IDs, and exact record facts.

00:01:55.001 --> 00:01:56.801
A note is none of those.

00:01:57.041 --> 00:02:00.141
A test rejects it in two hundred and twelve placements.

00:02:00.576 --> 00:02:05.256
On the server, the change is three files and about two hundred added lines.

00:02:06.752 --> 00:02:09.892
This is a prompt the gateway recorded on the live server,

00:02:10.112 --> 00:02:11.272
word for word.

00:02:11.612 --> 00:02:13.232
Codes and record facts.

00:02:13.512 --> 00:02:15.692
Not Dani’s name, not her note.

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:21.857
To verify it, a test puts a marker that exists nowhere else into a note,

00:02:21.937 --> 00:02:25.417
and confirms the advisor route returns the note unchanged.

00:02:26.017 --> 00:02:30.136
Then it searches for that marker in each prompt a spy on the model captured,

00:02:30.317 --> 00:02:33.947
the gateway’s log, the other replies, the server’s output,

00:02:33.977 --> 00:02:34.837
and the queue.

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:36.840
Now I break it on purpose.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:41.000
One added line hands the note straight to the model, around the gateway,

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.720
and swallows any error.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:47.310
The gateway’s log never records that call, so a scan of the log alone would miss

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:47.720
it.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.000
The spy does not miss it.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:53.940
The test fails, and names the marker inside a model prompt.

00:02:55.833 --> 00:02:59.333
The saved mutation run breaks the app one guard at a time,

00:02:59.493 --> 00:03:02.013
and every break made its test fail.

00:03:02.353 --> 00:03:04.573
This table lists the ones aimed at the note.

00:03:06.516 --> 00:03:09.256
A second model reviewed the plan and the code.

00:03:09.576 --> 00:03:12.376
The copy check in the gateway came from that review.

00:03:13.634 --> 00:03:17.874
The detector is Rampart Edge, from the US National Design Studio.

00:03:18.174 --> 00:03:20.414
It is itself a small AI model.

00:03:20.794 --> 00:03:24.884
Served from this site, it runs in the app only in the two browsers that already

00:03:24.914 --> 00:03:25.754
hold the note.

00:03:26.074 --> 00:03:29.334
The server runs no model on a note, not even this one.

00:03:29.874 --> 00:03:31.674
And it is not the boundary.

00:03:32.094 --> 00:03:37.014
On forty invented notes, it flagged nothing in the twelve about sensitive situations,

00:03:37.234 --> 00:03:42.634
a parent’s job loss, an eviction, a health worry, because they hold no identifier.

00:03:43.154 --> 00:03:48.664
Arjun raised a related limit on our call: a troubling sentence may match no crisis

00:03:48.694 --> 00:03:49.254
pattern.

00:03:49.614 --> 00:03:52.854
Finding identifiers cannot tell you a note is private.

00:03:54.153 --> 00:03:55.833
What this does not prove.

00:03:56.273 --> 00:03:59.113
The boundary has not met a real provider’s model.

00:03:59.453 --> 00:04:01.553
No test drives a real browser.

00:04:01.833 --> 00:04:04.973
The spy cannot see a model client it was not handed.

00:04:05.173 --> 00:04:07.453
And host logs are outside the repo.

00:04:07.993 --> 00:04:12.033
Production still needs sign-in, access limited to the assigned advisor,

00:04:12.333 --> 00:04:15.293
and an encrypted queue that survives a restart.

00:04:15.633 --> 00:04:16.953
Those are not built.

00:04:17.553 --> 00:04:18.433
One more gap.

00:04:18.893 --> 00:04:21.393
The crisis check is a list of patterns.

00:04:21.713 --> 00:04:25.453
Saying "I want to disappear" does not show the crisis card.

00:04:26.648 --> 00:04:31.308
The planner, the inbox, the report and the code are public at these links.

00:04:31.608 --> 00:04:32.568
Thank you both.
